  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q7-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Using the common logarithm, determine the number of digits that $2^{100}$ has.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$31$ digits.\n\nThe common logarithm lies between $30$ and $31$, so the number has $30+1$ digits.",
      "worked": "From the common logarithm table, $\\log_{10}2\\approx0.3010$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(2^{100})&=100\\log_{10}2\\\\\\log_{10}(2^{100})&\\approx100(0.3010)\\\\\\log_{10}(2^{100})&\\approx30.10\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $10^{30}<2^{100}<10^{31}$. A positive integer in this interval has $31$ digits.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
